      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why the split: a node's `sources` list every file it covers, which for a hub node is megabytes \u2014 unreadable\nin a context window and, symmetrically, unwritable from one. So the model never emits frontmatter and never\nreads a raw node: it decides the clustering (manifest.tsv) and writes the prose (b-NN.md), and the scripts do\neverything mechanical and fixed \u2014 enumerate, hash, digest, mirror, upload, verify.",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why the split: a node's `sources` list every file it covers, which for a hub node is megabytes \u2014 unreadable\nin a context window and, symmetrically, unwritable from one. So the model never emits frontmatter and never\nreads a raw node: it decides the clustering (manifest.tsv) and writes the prose (b-NN.md), and the scripts do\neverything mechanical and fixed \u2014 enumerate, hash, digest, mirror, upload, verify.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
